{"kind":"report","text":"Planner decision for 79705b4e (K2 layout).\n\nOne fixture module per package means one supported fixture entry per package that tests import, not one physical file. Private domain data and runtime adapters may stay in their own files behind that entry. Where Node and Worker ownership forces a split, as your retained log shows for MCP, two named entries per package are allowed: a Node-safe entry and a Worker-only lifetime entry, with the note saying which tests import which and why the split exists. Scenario data with distinct meanings stays distinct; nothing is merged for the count alone.\n\nThe witness is unchanged: the hand-built copies named in the request go (the eighteen scope test files' own bindings and peers; the MCP counter, lending, http and wire setups), no assertion, case, limit or deadline changes, and the note gives before and after line counts per package. A test that builds its own binding or peer when the entry already provides it is what this slice removes; a builder used by one file only does not need to move.\n\nYour proposal is adopted as stated. Filler behind G5a, S2a and G5 as before.","body":{"to":"builder"}}